            <ArticleTitle>Identification of orally-bioavailable antagonists of the TRPV4 ion-channel.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>4011-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.bmcl.2015.06.098</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0960-894X(15)00703-9</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Antagonists of the TRPV4 receptor were identified using a focused screen, followed by a limited optimization program. The leading compounds obtained from this exercise, RN-1665 23 and RN-9893 26, showed moderate oral bioavailability when dosed to rats. The lead molecule, RN-9893 26, inhibited human, rat and murine variants of TRPV4, and showed excellent selectivity over related TRP receptors, such as TRPV1, TRPV3 and TRPM8. The overall profile for RN-9893 may permit its use as a proof-of-concept probe for in vivo applications.</AbstractText>
